72 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 33 0 R
/E (As we gathered there, we prayed: "Bless the Lord, all you works of the Lord" \(Canticle of Daniel 3: 52-90\). We called upon the sun and moon, the stars of heaven, the seas and rivers, the birds of the air and all peoples of the earth to join in praise. It teaches us that creation is not simply a backdrop to our lives but a great choir proclaiming God's glory. Perhaps that is a fitting thought on this day when the feast of St Francis of Assisi quietly yields to the Sunday liturgy.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [41]
>>
endobj
73 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 33 0 R
/E (Saint Paul urges us to dwell on whatever is true, noble and good. When we see the world with grateful eyes, we bear the fruits God desires: compassion, justice, peace and love. Amen.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [42]
>>
endobj
74 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 33 0 R
/E (Standing in that little oratory, one is reminded of a truth that the Celtic spiritual tradition understood deeply: the whole of creation is charged with the presence of God. Nothing is merely ordinary. Everything speaks of the Creator.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [43]
>>
endobj
